docs[1]{path,scope}:
  README.md,project
body: "This item implements pending-only default git notes and tracks the read-only pm-context recovery investigation. Companion class: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cli-website-tbni.toon. Release failures: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cli-website-mcrq.toon.\n\nThe code PR is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/311. At code head 23fba9866b450673771242dbf929d72aea920e7a, lifecycle, Node 22, Node 26, CodeQL/codeql and Semgrep passed. Each Node job ran the full npm and Bun release gates: 985 tests, 985 pass, zero failures/skips; all 28 required source files measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Docstrings cover 264 declarations across 39 files. Production audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Thresholds are unchanged. Statements are not independently measured; pmc-ilrh tracks that separate metric. The source and extension add nine tests in total: eight standalone regression cases and one extension integration case.\n\nRevert evidence: the actual base ff74b2c97752ec6d12c11de51d95f9fee0c4608c, archived with the new tests and exact dependencies, gives 3 pass/5 fail; restored source gives 8 pass/0 fail. The committed disposable proof separately reverses the pending-default condition (4 failures, fixed/restored 8 pass) and removes the existing requested-release preflight (1 failure, fixed/restored 1 pass). The latter guard was already on main and is reused rather than duplicated.\n\npm-context evidence was read only after the code PR became green on 2026-11-02. Its main/prepared SHA is 2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63. The release commit subject is Release pm-context v2026.11.01; package, manifest, top-level lock and lock root package all say 2026.11.1. Preserve that normalized npm version and that zero-padded release tag spelling. No November release tag exists; npm latest is 2026.10.31 and a read of pm-context@2026.11.1 returns E404. CHANGELOG.md starts at 2026.10.31 and has no 2026.11.1 section.\n\nThe intended delivered window is v2026.10.31 (b145a0751c3831a28e08ec52c3cedd26e8fa999a), exclusive, through f20b9b2decdd0bbe28c4ed7a68543ee398171526. It contains exactly:\n\n- 1573c15fbcd7481398ff9a078f0c74ecb910b481: closeout reusable-workflow pin, PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/206.\n- f20b9b2decdd0bbe28c4ed7a68543ee398171526: sync reusable-workflow pin, PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/205.\n\nBoth uses refs move from pm-github 2026.10.19 (09412243e2543adedbb73a4f4b2f2b6e2ac0c8a6) to 2026.10.28 (1191c65f88bb9129c33e74a650afc8d9c0eae219). Their pm-github-version input stays 2026.10.16; do not describe this as a CLI package upgrade. The prepared metadata commit is not an additional delivered dependency change.\n\nAuthoritative sources:\n\n- Window: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/compare/v2026.10.31...f20b9b2decdd0bbe28c4ed7a68543ee398171526\n- Workflow: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63/.github/workflows/release.yml\n- CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n- Failed resume: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/41307066720/job/124849534845. Restore prepared release notes refused the missing section after immutable release verification.\n\nThe resume decision selects the oldest untagged Release pm-context v commit and validates its metadata. Verify merged release checks out that exact prepared SHA, reruns release:check and checks a clean rebuild. Restore prepared release notes then reads that checkout's CHANGELOG.md, not the mutable main tree. Only when the section is absent can an explicitly supplied recovery_notes_sha provide it. The input must be a full lowercase 40-hex SHA, descend from the prepared SHA, be contained in origin/main and contain the exact same-version heading. The awk extractor requires ## 2026.11.1 - followed by the date; the tag spelling v2026.11.01 is not the heading spelling.\n\nThere is a recovery-specific CI constraint: pm-context pins pm-changelog 2026.10.27 and CI runs its canonical full changelog check. Adding only a manual dependency section makes that check fail. An isolated clone at the exact prepared SHA, using that exact old generator and matching PM CLI peer, verified baseline canonical projection passes and the plain notes-only change fails. Merely rerunning release.yml without an authorized recovery SHA also repeats the refusal. Upgrading a dependency on current main would not change the immutable prepared artifact.\n\nThe smallest verified plan that keeps the existing canonical CI and immutable artifact contract is a two-commit recovery receipt PR in pm-context, after separate authorization:\n\n1. From the prepared main lineage, create commit A changing only CHANGELOG.md. Insert the same-version section below, preserving every older byte. Review its two bullets against the two immutable workflow diffs. A contains no runtime, version, lockfile or workflow changes and invents no closed release items.\n2. Create commit B restoring CHANGELOG.md byte for byte to its original canonical content and recording A's full SHA, the exact notes text/digest and window evidence on a real non-closed recovery tracker item with its history. This gives a reviewable receipt at the PR tip while retaining A's notes blob in history. Verify canonical changelog projection and all required CI on the final tip. No generator flag, dependency, workflow or threshold change is needed for this recovery.\n3. Merge in a way that preserves A as an ancestor of main. A squash that drops A is unsuitable. A normal merge commit is currently permitted; after any ancestry-preserving merge or rebase, identify the actual full notes-commit SHA on main and reverify its exact content. Do not assume an unmerged branch SHA is authorized. Verify prepared -> notes commit -> origin/main ancestry and the two-bullet same-version extraction.\n4. Only after separate execution authorization, dispatch release.yml on main with recovery_notes_sha set to that actual verified notes commit. The workflow must resume npm 2026.11.1 at prepared SHA 2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63, then publish/tag v2026.11.01 at that prepared SHA using its existing provenance, rebuild, registry reconciliation and Bun gates. The recovery SHA supplies GitHub release notes; it does not replace the artifact SHA. Do not select a newer calendar release or move a tag to a receipt commit.\n\nProposed notes in A:\n\n```markdown\n## 2026.11.1 - 2026-11-01\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- Bump the pm-github sync workflow pin from 2026.10.19 to 2026.10.28 ([#205](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/205)).\n- Bump the pm-github closeout workflow pin from 2026.10.19 to 2026.10.28 ([#206](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/206)).\n```\n\nRecovery proof was scratch-only with no remote writes: cloned the real prepared history, used pm-changelog 2026.10.27 to verify the original canonical projection, demonstrated the notes-only refusal, created synthetic A/B commits, verified the canonical receipt tip, detached back to the real prepared SHA and executed only the exact existing Restore prepared release notes shell block. It recovered exactly the proposed two bullets. Missing, short and sectionless recovery refs refused. No pm-context branch, tracker, dependency, workflow, tag, release or registry state was changed. No workflow was dispatched, no PR was merged and no release was performed. The future recovery SHA is deliberately unassigned: it must be a real post-approval main ancestor, never a synthetic proof SHA."
